<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashikaga Yoshiaki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1537–1597</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashikaga Yoshiaki was the fifteenth and last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> of the Ashikaga shogunate. After his brother was murdered in 1565 he sought shelter with the Asakura and others, and in 1568 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> marched into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> and installed him as shogun. Yoshiaki then plotted against his patron, and in 1573 Nobunaga expelled him from Kyoto, ending the shogunate in practice.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshiaki.jpg" alt="Ashikaga Yoshiaki" width="320" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 松平定信（編） · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashikaga_Yoshiaki2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
